2026-10-02T21:46:36.333Z [DEBUG] MCP server "claude.ai Refero": Connection established with capabilities: {"hasTools":true,"hasPrompts":true,"hasResources":true,"hasResourceSubscribe":false,"serverVersion":{"name":"refero_server","version":"0.2.0","description":"Refero is a design research MCP with visual styles, real interface screens, and complete user flows from strong digital products. Use it to ground design decisions in concrete references instead of generic model assumptions.\n\n- **Styles** (`refero_search_styles`, `refero_get_style`) help explore visual directions, techniques, and inspiration: typography, color, composition, spacing, surfaces, components, imagery, and art direction. They are especially useful for landing pages, marketing pages, product websites, and other brand-facing work.\n- **Screens** (`refero_search_screens`) come from a large searchable collection of real web and iOS interfaces. Search by page or screen type, product, company, component, pattern, state, visual detail, or on-screen text to find examples for almost any UI task. Use `refero_get_screen` for full details, `refero_get_similar_screens` for related examples, and `refero_get_screen_image` for image content.\n- **Flows** (`refero_search_flows`, `refero_get_flow`) show real user journeys as connected screens. Search by task, topic, product, company, industry, or key step to understand sequences, decisions, user actions, system responses, friction, recovery, and completion.\n\nInspect several relevant references and synthesize what fits the user's product instead of copying one source or averaging distinctive ideas into a generic middle.\n\nWhen installed, use the `refero-design` skill as the full design methodology. Tool descriptions provide detailed query guidance and usage constraints."},"protocolEra":"modern","negotiatedProtocolVersion":"2026-07-28"}
